# Fictional EP Tracklist

## 1. Return Stroke Lands Behind the Scale Bell

**Story & Context:** The debut runs at 132 BPM. Dilnoza opens with a four-note dutar cell whose DRIVE strokes land almost directly on the implied pulse while the RETURN strokes lean slightly late. Leon programs only kick, one clipped snare, and sparse hats, leaving the late RETURN attacks exposed as part of the groove.

After four cycles, Aziza answers every second RETURN with one damped prepared-piano fifth. Timur removes the corresponding digital rim hit and replaces it with a dry doira finger snap. Mara enters only after Dilnoza moves the figure up an octave, adding one low bass-oboe fourth beneath the now-opened register.

At the midpoint, Dilnoza reverses emphasis so RETURN becomes the stronger stroke. Leon responds by shifting a kick away from the DRIVE and placing it after the accented RETURN. The groove feels newly tilted without changing BPM. The final cycle ends with a light RETURN stroke and the faint mechanical bell of an old floor scale recorded in the room.

